\title{02 - Official Lean 4 kernel type checker core (v4.36.0): implementation-grade specification}
\taxon{Study}
\date{2026-11-23}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{queclr}
\tag{reference-engine}
\tag{levels}
\tag{nat}
\meta{origin}{docs/research/02-kernel-typechecker.md}
\meta{moved}{2026-11-24}
\import{base-macros}

\p{Scope: everything in the official C++ kernel except declaration admission (inductive checking, recursor generation, replay order), which the declaration-admission document covers. All paths are relative to \code{\verb~|refs/~}. Line numbers refer to \code{\verb~|lean4~} at tag \code{\verb~|v4.36.0~} (commit \code{\verb~|611c117~}). "throw" always means a kernel exception, i.e. the whole declaration is rejected.}

\p{Notation: \code{\verb~|==~} structural equality (binder names/infos ignored, see 2.3); \code{\verb~|=p~} pointer equality; \code{\verb~|whnf_core(e, cheap_proj)~} = \code{\verb~|whnf_core(e, cheap_rec=false, cheap_proj)~}.}

