\subtree{
\title{11. Performance-relevant behaviour (what Mathlib and the perf tests rely on)}

\table{
\tr{\th{Behaviour}\th{Where}\th{What goes wrong without it}\th{Arena perf test}}
\tr{\td{Structural equality / success-pair test before any reduction}\td{\code{\verb~|quick_is_def_eq~}}\td{identical nested terms unfolded pairwise, exponential}\td{\code{\verb~|identical-nesting~}, \code{\verb~|repeated-subproblem~}}}
\tr{\td{Same regular head: compare arguments (last to first) before unfolding; cache the failure}\td{8.4}\td{Theta(n^2) instead of Theta(n); without the failure cache the same failed argument comparison repeats at every level}\td{\code{\verb~|args-before-unfold~}, \code{\verb~|proj-stuck-struct~}}}
\tr{\td{Unfold the definition with the greater height; abbrev before regular; never a theorem while a definition is available}\td{\code{\verb~|compare~}}\td{evaluating the cheap-to-match side to normal form}\td{\code{\verb~|unroll-versus-evaluate~}, \code{\verb~|loop-unfolded-once~}}}
\tr{\td{Proof irrelevance before delta, with a definitive negative answer}\td{8.3}\td{evaluating proofs (e.g. well-founded recursion witnesses)}\td{\code{\verb~|irrelevance-refutes~}, \code{\verb~|irrelevance-before-evaluation~}}}
\tr{\td{Cheap projection mode first; lazy lockstep unfolding under equal projections}\td{8.1 step 3, 8.5}\td{reducing a structure to a constructor when its arguments already agree}\td{\code{\verb~|proj-cheap-struct~}, \code{\verb~|proj-lazy-struct~}}}
\tr{\td{Stuck projection keeps the folded struct term}\td{7.1}\td{the folded head is lost and recursion trees unroll, exponential}\td{\code{\verb~|proj-stuck-struct~}}}
\tr{\td{When only one side is delta and the other is a stuck projection application, reduce the projection instead}\td{8.4 "only dt"}\td{lazily unfolding an expensive term against an instance projection}\td{(comment at \code{\verb~|type_checker.cpp:968-975~})}}
\tr{\td{Nat folding in def-eq only on fvar-free sides; let variables are fvars}\td{8.4, 6.6}\td{evaluating a let-bound closed term that never needed evaluation}\td{\code{\verb~|let-fold~}}}
\tr{\td{Infer cache on shared sub-DAGs, separate check/infer-only}\td{5}\td{2^n re-inference}\td{\code{\verb~|app-lam~}}}
\tr{\td{Telescoped binder traversal (one instantiation per binder group), multi-argument beta, infer-only spine walk}\td{6.3-6.6, section 4}\td{Theta(n^2) substitution on ladders}\td{\code{\verb~|beta-ladder~}, \code{\verb~|let-ladder~}, \code{\verb~|shift-cascade~}, \code{\verb~|app-lam~}}}
\tr{\td{O(1) loose-bvar range as dependency test in \code{\verb~|infer_proj~}}\td{6.8}\td{Theta(N^3) for wide Prop structures}\td{\code{\verb~|prop-struct-projections~}}}
\tr{\td{GMP arithmetic on literals, binary literals never unary}\td{7.6}\td{infeasible}\td{\code{\verb~|gf3-matrix-product~}, \code{\verb~|other/nat-lit-*~}}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|m_unfold~}: instantiated bodies of universe-polymorphic constants reused}\td{5}\td{re-instantiating large bodies at every unfold}\td{-}}
\tr{\td{Hash-consing of theorem type/value before checking}\td{\code{\verb~|environment.cpp:196-198~}}\td{pointer-keyed traversal memo and \code{\verb~|=p~} fast paths miss}\td{-}}
}

\p{Known weak spots of the official strategy (RLVM may do better without changing verdicts): arguments are compared before unfolding even if the head ignores them (\code{\verb~|discarded-argument~}, \code{\verb~|short-circuit-and~}: about 14 s); Nat folding is tried before unfolding on closed terms (\code{\verb~|unfold-before-literal~}: about 20 s); the higher side is unfolded even when one step on the lower side would finish (\code{\verb~|ite-taken-branch~}); applied projections are reduced eagerly (\code{\verb~|proj-applied-struct~}, \code{\verb~|proj-app-lazy-delta~}); whnf caches retain every big literal until the declaration ends (\code{\verb~|gf3-matrix-product~}: 3.5 GiB). The official kernel needs about 33.7 minutes of virtual time for Mathlib, so mirroring it literally (substitution-based, per-declaration caches) is not the performance target; mirroring its \em{decisions} is.}

\p{Implications for an NbE/closure design (design guidance, not verified facts):}

\ul{
\li{Neutral values need the folded form (constant + argument thunks) next to the unfolded continuation, so that 8.4 can compare arguments and consult hints before forcing ("glued" evaluation).}
\li{Proof irrelevance and unit eta need the type of an arbitrary value; either carry types on neutrals or quote and re-infer. They must be consulted before delta unfolding.}
\li{The \code{\verb~|hasFVar~} guard needs a cheap "closed" bit on values/thunks; let-bound variables count as open.}
\li{A cache on open values must include the environment (levels included) and the mode, see rows 18-19.}
\li{The official recursion depth is bounded only by the native stack; Mathlib terms nest deeply, so the JVM checker threads need a large explicit stack size or an explicit work stack.}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{12. Changes on master after v4.36.0 (diff \code{\verb~|v4.36.0..7e19442~})}

\ol{
\li{\code{\verb~|is_def_eq_core~}: \code{\verb~|is_def_eq_proof_irrel(t, s)~} moved in front of the first \code{\verb~|whnf_core~}.}
\li{\code{\verb~|inductive_reduce_rec~}: \code{\verb~|if (!is_prop(infer_type(major))) major = whnf(major)~}; proof majors are no longer normalised (related tests: \code{\verb~|corner-cases/eta-struct-major-no-whnf~}, \code{\verb~|-and-no-whnf~}).}
\li{\code{\verb~|to_cnstr_when_structure~}: the Prop test is replaced by "recursor is not large-eliminating" (\code{\verb~|#lparams(rec) == #lparams(first inductive of the block)~} -> no eta), enabling eta for \code{\verb~|And~}-like majors.}
\li{\code{\verb~|try_eta_struct_core~}: a partially applied constructor of a structure is eta-expanded with fresh fvars taken from the constructor application's own type (the variant that \code{\verb~|bugs/eta-ctor-alias~} demands).}
\li{Projection indices are \code{\verb~|size_t~}; open-addressing pointer-pair sets replace \code{\verb~|std::unordered_set~} in \code{\verb~|expr_eq_fn~}/\code{\verb~|for_each_fn~}; \code{\verb~|replace_fn~} rewritten. No change to levels.}
}

\p{Changes 1, 3 and 4 let the kernel accept more (or answer earlier); the affected arena tests have outcome "either". Change 2 also makes it accept LESS (inference from the code, not run): a recursor of a non-structure Prop inductive, e.g. \code{\verb~|Acc.rec~}, no longer fires when its major is a proof that must be unfolded to become a constructor application (as in \code{\verb~|WellFounded.fix~} through \code{\verb~|WellFounded.apply~}). Keeping the v4.36 behaviour (whnf of every major) therefore accepts a superset of master here, at the price of non-termination on the two \code{\verb~|-no-whnf~} corner cases (60 s timeout, outcome "either").}
}

\subtree{
\title{13. Not verified, and open questions}

\ul{
\li{Which hint kind the elaborator assigns to instances and structure projection functions (only the kernel side of hints was read).}
\li{Whether the Mathlib v4.36.0 export contains \code{\verb~|mdata~} nodes, \code{\verb~|nondep~} lets or \code{\verb~|partial~} constants (export format is covered by another document).}
\li{PR numbers are quoted from the arena test descriptions and \code{\verb~|lean4lean/divergences.md~}; only the resulting code at the four tags and master was inspected.}
\li{Behaviour of the official checker on \code{\verb~|Nat.pow~}/\code{\verb~|Nat.shiftLeft~} guard violations beyond reading the code (no binary was run).}
\li{Open: primitive validation. An export that declares \code{\verb~|Nat.add~} (or \code{\verb~|Nat~}, \code{\verb~|Bool.true~}, \code{\verb~|String.ofList~}) with a non-standard body makes the literal extension disagree with delta unfolding; by the code read here and by \code{\verb~|lean4lean/divergences.md~} the official checker accepts such a file (not run). Validating the definitional behaviour of the 15 Nat functions and of the literal constants (as lean4lean does) closes this, at the cost of rejecting exports the official checker accepts.}
\li{Open: whether guard violations of 7.6 (\code{\verb~|Nat.pow~} exponent above 2^32-1, or above 2^24 for a word-sized base; numerals above 128 MiB) should be mirrored as "reject" or reported as "decline". None of the arena test descriptions read for this document exercises them.}
\li{Open: caches that outlive one declaration are not what the official kernel does. For closed terms they are sound (the environment only grows and constants never change), but memory then has to be bounded explicitly; the official kernel frees everything after each declaration.}
}
}
